        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Leigh Silverman, Jeanine Tesori, Brian Crawley, Doris Betts\n- Works: Violet, From Up Here, The Ugliest Pilgrim\n- Roles: stage director, composer, librettist, author\n- Awards: Tony Award, Drama Desk Award\n\nFacts:\n- Leigh Silverman is an American stage director who has worked both Off-Broadway and on Broadway.\n- Leigh Silverman was nominated for the 2008 Drama Desk Award for Outstanding Director of a Play for From Up Here.\n- Leigh Silverman was nominated for the 2014 Tony Award for Best Direction of a Musical for Violet.\n- Violet is a musical with music by Jeanine Tesori and a libretto by Brian Crawley.\n- Violet is based on the short story The Ugliest Pilgrim by Doris Betts.",
